--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FFmpeg
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

KiteFFmpeg is a binding. It contains no FFmpeg source, and this repository ships no
FFmpeg binaries in its git tree. FFmpeg is NOT covered by this NOTICE or by
KiteFFmpeg's Apache-2.0 licence.

Since 2026-08-22, KiteFFmpeg's PUBLISHED ARTIFACTS (the per-target
klibs, the JVM jar's bundled native library, and the Android AAR's JNI
libraries) EMBED compiled FFmpeg with the dav1d AV1 decoder. Those FFmpeg
portions remain LGPL-2.1-or-later (dav1d: BSD-2-Clause); the artifact POMs
declare all three licences, the JVM jar carries the licence texts under
META-INF/licenses/kiteffmpeg-ffmpeg/, and the complete corresponding FFmpeg
source is attached to the `ffmpeg-<version>` GitHub release, which is the single
canonical home for it (the binaries are keyed to the FFmpeg version, not to
KiteFFmpeg's, so every KiteFFmpeg release points at the same one). An application
that ships these artifacts must give its users the LGPL notice and keep that
source available; that release asset satisfies the source half.

The binaries this project builds (its GitHub Release assets, and the trees its
build tasks produce) are built from unmodified FFmpeg release sources at the
version pinned in gradle.properties, configured WITHOUT --enable-gpl and without
any GPL-only component. They are covered by the GNU Lesser General Public License,
version 2.1 or later.

  FFmpeg          https://ffmpeg.org
  LGPL v2.1       https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/lgpl-2.1.html
  Source          https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg at the pinned tag, unmodified
                  apart from the patches under native/patches/ffmpeg, which are
                  committed in this repository

As of 0.1.0 this project builds and publishes NO GPL flavour. x264 and x265 are
never linked here. A tree you build yourself with --enable-gpl is yours, and its
obligations are yours.

WHAT THIS MEANS IF YOU SHIP AN APP USING KITECODEC

  - The LGPL applies to FFmpeg, not to your application, and not to KiteFFmpeg's
    own Apache-2.0 code.
  - State that your application uses FFmpeg under the LGPL, and make the
    corresponding FFmpeg source available to your users. Linking to the tag above
    plus any patches you applied satisfies this.
  - If you link FFmpeg statically, the LGPL additionally requires that your users
    be able to relink your application against a modified FFmpeg. Publishing your
    object files, or providing a written offer, are the usual routes.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Components the published artifacts actually contain
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This list was read out of the shipped lib/ directories, not from a configure
line, and it is complete for every artifact this project publishes.

  FFmpeg          LGPL-2.1-or-later   https://ffmpeg.org
                  (the eight libav* libraries, bundled)
  dav1d           BSD-2-Clause        https://code.videolan.org/videolan/dav1d
                  (bundled; it is the software AV1 decoder)
  zlib            zlib                https://zlib.net
                  (linked from the platform SDK or the system, not bundled)

Nothing else is linked. In particular there is no SVT-AV1, libvpx, libaom,
libopus, libmp3lame, libwebp, libass, FreeType, HarfBuzz or FriBidi in any
published artifact. A wider "fat" desktop profile enabled several of those and
was removed on 2026-08-22, because it could not produce a self-contained
artifact.

